    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d783">

                <pb facs="0729" n="557" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg557"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/4134</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Norway</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Schmedeman</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Christiania</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-28T15:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 28, 1917, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 4.20 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>166. Department’s circular of March 16, 2 p.m. I have received from the Minister
                    for Foreign Affairs a note dated April 26 in which he states that “the Norwegian
                    Government is obliged to reserve to itself the right to make a decision in each
                    separate case where a merchant vessel belonging to a belligerent power and with
                    such an armed guard on board might enter a Norwegian port.”</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Schmedeman</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
